      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a very clear perspective. You mentioned \"subject races\" that benefit from \"enlightened governance.\" When you're dealing with the local population on the ground, how do you actually view their capacity for self-governance? Is there a fundamental difference in temperament or intellect that makes British oversight so vital compared to their own ability to manage themselves?",
